[CENTER][IMG]BASE_URL/banner.png[/IMG]

[SIZE=5][B]Record what your players see. Replay it in game.[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Packet-based replays for Spigot 1.8.8 and Paper 26.3, with a developer API.[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[IMG]BASE_URL/header-features.png[/IMG]

[IMG]BASE_URL/features.png[/IMG]

[IMG]BASE_URL/header-how-it-works.png[/IMG]

[IMG]BASE_URL/how-it-works.png[/IMG]

ClaudeReplay records the packets received by each player in a world, together with the block changes. Replays never contain the world itself: when a replay is watched, its base map (by default [FONT=Courier New]plugins/ClaudeReplay/maps/<mapId>[/FONT]) is copied into a temporary world and the recorded changes are applied on top of it.

[IMG]BASE_URL/header-versions.png[/IMG]

[IMG]BASE_URL/versions.png[/IMG]

Replays recorded on 1.8.8 are converted to the modern protocol while they play. Paintings, signs, maps, entity attributes and particles carrying a block or an item have no modern equivalent and are skipped.

[IMG]BASE_URL/header-commands.png[/IMG]

[IMG]BASE_URL/commands.png[/IMG]

[B]Permissions:[/B] [FONT=Courier New]claudereplay.record[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]claudereplay.play[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]claudereplay.admin[/FONT] (includes both).
Viewers also get hotbar items: points of view, markers, backward, play / pause, forward, speed, controls and leave.

[IMG]BASE_URL/header-api.png[/IMG]

[CODE=Java]ClaudeReplayAPI api = ClaudeReplayProvider.get();

Recording recording = api.startRecording(RecordingOptions.builder(arena.getWorld())
        .name("BedWars #" + gameId)
        .mapId("bedwars_lighthouse")
        .metadata("game", "bedwars")
        .build());

recording.addMarker("Red bed destroyed");

recording.stop().thenAccept(replay -> broadcast("Replay saved: " + replay.id()));[/CODE]

Events ([FONT=Courier New]RecordingStartEvent[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]RecordingPlayerAddEvent[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]PlaybackStartEvent[/FONT]…), playback control, custom storage ([FONT=Courier New]ReplayStorage[/FONT]) and custom map sources ([FONT=Courier New]MapResolver[/FONT]) are documented in the README.

[IMG]BASE_URL/header-installation.png[/IMG]

[LIST=1]
[*]Install [URL='https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/packetevents-api.80279/']packetevents[/URL] 2.14.0 or newer.
[*]Drop [B]ClaudeReplay.jar[/B] into your [FONT=Courier New]plugins[/FONT] folder.
[*]Put the base maps of your recorded worlds in [FONT=Courier New]plugins/ClaudeReplay/maps/<mapId>[/FONT].
[/LIST]
[B]Requirements:[/B] Paper 26.3 (Java 25) or Spigot 1.8.8 running on Java 17+.
